Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/exabit-io/pitch

Package: pitch
Architecture: amd64 arm64 riscv64 loong64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, procps
Description: run a command at a higher or lower CPU frequency (inverse of nice)
 nice changes how much CPU time a process gets; pitch changes how fast the CPU
 runs while the process has it. It sets the scheduler's per-task utilization
 clamps, which the schedutil cpufreq governor follows: pitch +20 runs a task
 (and its children) at the top frequency wherever it is scheduled, so serial
 work such as package builds stops waiting for the governor to ramp up;
 negative pitches cap background work near the lowest frequency. -b adds
 idle CPU scheduling and idle I/O priority for a one-flag background tier.
 .
 Any user may set the pitch of their own processes. Needs a kernel with
 utilization clamping and the schedutil governor (on Intel:
 intel_pstate=passive).
 .
 schedutil-setup (in /usr/sbin) puts a machine on that policy and keeps it
 there: passive driver mode and schedutil on the kernel command line, the
 realtime clamp fix (kernel.sched_util_clamp_min_rt_default=0), a pin for
 cpufrequtils, conflict checks, verify after reboot, and uninstall.
